    "question": "Which of the following statements correctly characterizes a tree in an undirected graph?",
    "options": {
      "A": "A connected graph with exactly one cycle",
      "B": "A connected acyclic graph",
      "C": "A graph where every vertex has degree 2",
      "D": "A graph that contains a Hamiltonian path"
    },
    "correct_answer": "B",
    "explanation": "A tree is defined as a connected graph with no cycles (acyclic). Option B matches this definition.",
    "difficulty": "Medium"
