    "question": "Given the adjacency matrix A of a simple undirected graph, which of the following statements is always true?",
    "options": {
      "A": "A is symmetric and its diagonal entries are all 1",
      "B": "A is symmetric and its diagonal entries are all 0",
      "C": "A is antisymmetric and its diagonal entries are all 0",
      "D": "A is upper‑triangular and may have non‑zero diagonal entries"
    },
    "correct_answer": "B",
    "explanation": "For a simple undirected graph, the adjacency matrix is symmetric because edges are bidirectional, and there are no loops, so diagonal entries are 0.",
    "difficulty": "Medium"
  }
